              "failure": {
                "kind": "verification_failed",
                "failure_class": "bad_output",
                "evidence": "review changes_requested: Distinct Plays within the same second are collapsed in duetflow/collector.py: collector.collect passes played_at through models.to_iso(), which serializes with timespec=\"seconds\". With the same track at 2026-01-01T10:00:00.100Z and 2026-01-01T10:00:00.900Z, the Collection reports and stores one row instead of two because both become 2026-01-01T10:00:00+00:00. This loses listening evidence and violates the requirement that a one-off Collection store its Plays and that idempotency be based on the full (role, track_id, played_at) natural key.; The phase's public Collection command is still a stub in duetflow/app.py. Running `python -m duetflow.app collect` prints that the command arrives in phase 02-collector-schema and exits 2, so the implemented collector cannot be run manually as docs/PLAN.md requires for this phase or later by the declared timer command.; duetflow/collector.py never checks the last successful Collection against collection.max_collection_gap_minutes and emits no warning. With an existing successful run older than 90 minutes, a Collection proceeds with empty stdout/stderr, hiding the plan's explicitly identified condition that Plays may already have been irrecoverably lost.; The new risky-file path duetflow/spotify.py:recently_played bypasses the data-endpoint response policy required by docs/PLAN.md section 5. Concrete 401, 429 with Retry-After: 1, and 500 responses each make exactly one request and immediately raise SpotifyError; there is no one-time token refresh, bounded Retry-After/quota handling, or exponential 5xx retry. Routine token expiry, rate limiting, or transient Spotify failure therefore loses that hourly Collection instead of following the mandated recovery behavior.",
                "retry_after_sec": null,
                "reset_at": null
              },
              "stepped_down": null,
              "impl_log": "/home/dan/projects/duetflow/.orchestrator/attempts/att_run_LisIoqe6p1xbHQj2_proof_review_01/impl.log",
