                "findings": [
                  "Distinct Plays within the same second are collapsed in duetflow/collector.py: collector.collect passes played_at through models.to_iso(), which serializes with timespec=\"seconds\". With the same track at 2026-01-01T10:00:00.100Z and 2026-01-01T10:00:00.900Z, the Collection reports and stores one row instead of two because both become 2026-01-01T10:00:00+00:00. This loses listening evidence and violates the requirement that a one-off Collection store its Plays and that idempotency be based on the full (role, track_id, played_at) natural key.",
                  "The phase's public Collection command is still a stub in duetflow/app.py. Running `python -m duetflow.app collect` prints that the command arrives in phase 02-collector-schema and exits 2, so the implemented collector cannot be run manually as docs/PLAN.md requires for this phase or later by the declared timer command.",
                  "duetflow/collector.py never checks the last successful Collection against collection.max_collection_gap_minutes and emits no warning. With an existing successful run older than 90 minutes, a Collection proceeds with empty stdout/stderr, hiding the plan's explicitly identified condition that Plays may already have been irrecoverably lost.",
